# Security

- Hash passwords with a strong algorithm (e.g. bcrypt/argon2); never store plaintext
- JWT/session secrets only from env; rotate guidance in ops docs when relevant
- CSRF strategy for cookie-based sessions; CORS allowlist — no `*` with credentials
- Sanitize/escape output; parameterized SQL only
- Upload allowlists (MIME + extension + size); serve with safe Content-Type
- Rate-limit login and password-reset
- Do not log secrets, payment proofs contents, or full card/OTP data
- Principle of least privilege for admin/staff roles
